  "title": "Consonants review 1: look-alikes",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "Review 1 of 2: look-alikes. No new letters.\n\n**Shape look-alikes**: ব (triangle) vs র (triangle + dot); ধ (open top-left) vs থ (bottom loop) vs য; উ (vowel) vs ড (notch in the top line); ড vs ড়, ঢ vs ঢ় and য vs য় (the dot!).\n\n**Sound-alikes**: জ/য, ন/ণ, শ/ষ/স and ঙ/ং sound the same. You can't hear the difference, so learn each word's spelling.\n\n**Hard vs soft**: ট/ড (tongue curled back) vs ত/দ (tongue on the teeth).",
